@rag = http://localhost:5070
# Paste a fresh token from the CoreAPI login: raw value only, no quotes, no "Bearer".
@token = PASTE_TOKEN_HERE

### A. Upload a Word agreement (same endpoint as PDF; .docx is accepted now)
POST {{rag}}/api/v1/vendor-agreements
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----RagBoundary

------RagBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="vendorId"

1
------RagBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="title"

Supply agreement 2026 (Word)
------RagBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="agreement.docx"
Content-Type: application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document

< C:\path\to\agreement.docx
------RagBoundary--

### B. Several questions as a list (structured + unstructured mixed)
POST {{rag}}/api/v1/agent/ask
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "questions": [
    "What are the payment terms of VEND004?",
    "How many purchase orders does VEND004 have and what is their total value?",
    "Which vendors have Net 45 payment terms?"
  ]
}

### C. One message containing two questions
POST {{rag}}/api/v1/agent/ask
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": "What is the warranty period for Summit Technology Services and when does its agreement end?" }
# For more info on HTTP files go to https://aka.ms/vs/httpfile
